  "showTitle": "The Hard Saying",
  "title": "Labor",
  "dates": "Saturday, September 5 – Monday, September 7, 2009",
  "logline": "Labor Day weekend: Theo kidnaps half of Delgado Hall to his father’s beach house in Malibu, where the gumbo takes an hour, the father takes six minutes, and somebody has to explain the dignity of labor.",
  "previously": [
    {
      "text": "Adrian Hale told the seminar a soul is just an inheritance. You told him he’d inherited his atheism too.",
      "if": "e2_soul_final==\"press\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Then he paired you with Lena for the semester. Her red ink in your margin: *Cite me.*"
    },
    {
      "text": "She told you about Wes — the boat, the storm, sixteen. You told her you’d been worried she had bad taste.",
      "if": "e2_wes_reply==\"honest\""
    },
    {
      "text": "You offered her the whole pack. She said she collects them one at a time — and that she’d need a container.",
      "if": "e2_cig_lena==\"offered\""
    },
    {
      "text": "You took a job washing dishes on the harbor, and a loan from Theo, payable in pie.",
      "if": "e2_books==\"loan\""
    },
    {
      "text": "Under a full moon, Theo said Los Angeles was three hours away. You told him you couldn’t afford it.",
      "if": "e2_la==\"broke\""
    }
  ],
